# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Easiest way to find them: press the "Connect" button at the top of your
# Supabase project dashboard. It shows both values ready to copy.
# They are also under Settings -> API Keys.
#
# The key is called the "publishable key" and starts with sb_publishable_ .
# Older projects call the same thing the "anon public" key instead; either
# works here, so paste whichever one your dashboard shows.
#
# .env.local is ignored by Git, so these never get published.
#
# This key is DESIGNED to be public and is visible in the browser on every
# Supabase site. It is not a password. What anyone can actually read or
# write is decided by the security rules in supabase/schema.sql.
#
# Never put the "secret" key (sb_secret_...) or the old "service_role" key
# in here. Those bypass every security rule.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
